<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andreas Victor Michiels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1797">1797</a>–<a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andreas Victor Michiels was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> general who served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>. He led campaigns in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> in the 1830s and 1840s and commanded the third Dutch military expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> in 1849, which took Jagaraga in Buleleng. Advancing on Klungkung, he was mortally wounded in a night attack at Kusamba in May 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andreas-victor-michiels.jpg" alt="Andreas Victor Michiels" width="320" height="359" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: W.R. van Hoevell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Michiels,_AV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
